r"""va_tfgd_breastcancer_viz.py

VA‑TFGD (Champion, theory-aligned) — Breast Cancer ONLY + Visualizations
======================================================================

This single-file script is tailored for your preferred scope: Breast Cancer Wisconsin only.
It is aligned with the manuscript Algorithm (VA‑TFGD, champion variant):
  q_t = tau q_{t-1} + (1-tau) ||g_t||^2
  buffer V (length W) of ||g_t||^2; bar_v = mean(V)
  lambda_target = lambda_base + c * tanh(bar_v)
  lambda_t = clip( tau*lambda_{t-1} + (1-tau)*lambda_target , [lam_min, lam_max])
  beta_t = exp(-lambda_t)
  v_t = g_t + beta_t v_{t-1}
  theta_{t+1} = theta_t - lr * v_t

What it does:
  - Runs Breast Cancer with stratified split (80/10/10 or 70/15/15)
  - Multi-seed evaluation (default seeds: 42..46)
  - Baselines: VA‑TFGD (Champion), TFGD(Fixed), SGD, SGD-M, Adam
  - Saves CSV outputs:
      results_dir/breastcancer_per_seed.csv
      results_dir/breastcancer_summary.csv
      results_dir/training_curves.csv
      results_dir/lambda_history_seedXX.csv (VA‑TFGD only)
  - Generates figures (PNG) in results_dir:
      fig_accuracy_bar.png
      fig_f1_bar.png
      fig_auc_bar.png
      fig_val_loss_curves.png
      fig_lambda_evolution.png
      fig_lambda_vs_gradnorm2.png

Colab usage:
  !pip -q install scikit-learn
  !python va_tfgd_breastcancer_viz.py --split 80/10/10 --seeds 42,43,44,45,46 --out_dir results_bc

Notes:
  - Colab/Jupyter safe: parse_known_args() ignores injected '-f kernel.json'.
"""

